{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1377157-sic-semper-tyrannis-thus-fall-tyrants","id":1377157,"title":"Sic Semper Tyrannis (Thus Fall Tyrants)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-29T05:22:57-07:00","id":1377157,"title":"Sic Semper Tyrannis (Thus Fall Tyrants)","content":"This is what John Wilkes Booth said when he shot Lincoln. For real.<br /> <br /> Sic Semper Tyrannis is a 16 page sourcebook you can buy from Storyteller\u2019s Vault. It\u2019s like an unofficial 2nd ed supplement to Requiem for Rome. If you liked Dark Eras, you should definitely buy this book (it\u2019s only four dollars). I love the quote from Julius Caesar: \u201cIf you must break the law, do it to seize power; in all other cases observe it.\u201d If Julia (my Ventrue character) lived in the Roman Requiem, this would\u2019ve been her motto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T08:07:05-07:00","id":1377177,"title":"","content":"Can you sum up what in this book is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T09:02:25-07:00","id":1377183,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s about the year of the Four Emperors (CE 69), when there were four Roman emperors. It\u2019s also about how the Julii and their mortal family lose control of Rome. And it has some stuff updating the various factions of the Camarilla to V:tR 2e. And a new Mekhet bloodline called the Flavians who use a variant form of Theban Sorcery and who think the Roman emperor Vespasian and his sons are semi-divine Christ figures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T16:25:31-07:00","id":1377814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1377157-sic-semper-tyrannis-thus-fall-tyrants#post1377157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what John Wilkes Booth said when he shot Lincoln. For real.<br /> <br /> Sic Semper Tyrannis is a 16 page sourcebook you can buy from Storyteller\u2019s Vault. It\u2019s like an unofficial 2nd ed supplement to Requiem for Rome. If you liked Dark Eras, you should definitely buy this book (it\u2019s only four dollars). I love the quote from Julius Caesar: \u201cIf you must break the law, do it to seize power; in all other cases observe it.\u201d If Julia (my Ventrue character) lived in the Roman Requiem, this would\u2019ve been her motto.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a link in the first post?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/